  - microdata
  - k-anonymity
  - referential integrity
abstract: >-
  oissyntheticdata is a zero-dependency, pure-Python tool, the single file
  gov_one.py, for offices whose confidential data is a folder of Excel and CSV
  files. On the premises it profiles the folder into aggregate-only JSON files:
  counts, shares and rounded quantiles, with no count below a minimum (5 by
  default), dates by month and weekday only, and identifiers described by shape
  only. Off the premises the same file rebuilds synthetic files from the JSON
  alone, with the same file names, sheets, headers, row counts and links
  between tables, and similar distributions; it never reads the confidential
  rows. An analyst writes a statistics script on the synthetic files with the
  built-in toolbox, and the same script is then run unchanged on the real files
  on the premises. Results from synthetic files test the script; they are not
  findings. Version 3 replaces the four-stage tool of versions 2.x and is not
  compatible with it. Maintained by OIS.
